{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"]}],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"KeyValueStore","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a small protocol for one-shot scalar values that don’t fit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" model. Three implementations ship:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore"},{"text":" — production, backed by any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"text":" suite","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"text":" — production, backed by the system Keychain (survives reinstall)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore"},{"text":" — tests, dictionary-backed, reference semantics","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject through your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Environment"},{"type":"text","text":", hydrate state at startup, and write from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effects. Reducers stay pure."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public protocol KeyValueStore: Sendable {","    func value<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Value?","    func setValue<Value>(_ value: Value?, for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func removeValue<Value>(for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func contains<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Bool","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All values are JSON-encoded as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":". Reads and writes go through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which pairs a backing-store name with its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" value type at compile time."}]},{"anchor":"When-to-Use-What","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"When to Use What"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Need"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Collection of identifiable entities (decks, cards, sessions)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scalar preference (theme, sort order, last-seen version)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (UserDefaults)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anonymous device identity that must survive reinstall"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (Keychain)"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is for many-of-a-kind data with change tracking and batched"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is for one-of-a-kind values that you read once at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"startup and overwrite on change."}]},{"anchor":"UserDefaults-vs-Keychain","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"UserDefaults vs Keychain"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Survives reinstall?"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes (this-device-only by default)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Backup \/ device migration"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Included"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Excluded with default accessibility"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Throughput"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fast (in-memory cache)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Slower (system call)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Visible to other apps?"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No (per app\/group)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Optionally (App Groups via "},{"code":"accessGroup:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Best for"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Theme, sort order, feature toggles, last-seen version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anonymous device ID, opaque tokens"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Keychain costs more per access — hydrate once at launch and observe state","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterward, never read inside a reducer."}]},{"anchor":"macOS-sandbox--entitlements","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"macOS sandbox & entitlements"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the data-protection keychain, so it never raises"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user prompt — no “Always Allow \/ Deny” dialog, no locked-keychain prompt, no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Touch ID \/ Face ID challenge."}]},{"style":"tip","type":"aside","name":"Tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"sandboxed","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" macOS app still needs a keychain entitlement, even when"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"not sharing items across an access group. Xcode supplies an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"application-identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically for provisioning-profile–signed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"builds; otherwise add an explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["<key>keychain-access-groups<\/key>","<array>","    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.example.myapp<\/string>","<\/array>"],"syntax":"xml","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without it, the first ","type":"text"},{"code":"setValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fails with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"errSecMissingEntitlement"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OSStatus"},{"type":"text","text":" −34018). This is a build\/signing condition, not a runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"prompt. iOS \/ iPadOS \/ tvOS \/ watchOS need no extra entitlement.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encryption, accessibility, iCloud-sync exclusion, and backup exclusion are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identical whichever entitlement you use — the access group only controls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"which of your own apps","type":"text"}]},{"text":" can read an item, never third parties or the cloud.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a private device ID, in order of strictness:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most private:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" profile-signed build + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup: nil"},{"type":"text","text":", relying on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application-identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" group. No other app — even same-team —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be entitled to it. Mirrors the iOS default; zero sharing surface."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Practically equivalent:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array whose only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"entry is the team-prefixed bundle id (the snippet above). Use when a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"profile-signed build isn’t available (unsigned local \/ CI dev). Only delta:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a same-team app you sign could also declare that string.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intentional sharing only:"}]},{"text":" a shared group string. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first"}]},{"text":" element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"becomes the default group for new items — never put a shared group first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for private data.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"anchor":"Device-Identity-Pattern","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Device-Identity Pattern"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The original motivation for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" was apps without user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"auth that still want stable identity for analytics. Stash a UUID once, hydrate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at launch, feed it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let deviceID = KVKey<String>(\"device-id\")","}","","\/\/ In Store.configured(), before constructing the store:","let kv = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")","let deviceID = kv.value(.deviceID) ?? {","    let new = UUID().uuidString","    kv.setValue(new, for: .deviceID)","    return new","}()","","let initialState = AppState(deviceID: deviceID, \/* … *\/)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Then in the analytics plugin wiring:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["AnalyticsPlugin(","    service: analytics,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, properties: { _ in [:] }),","    \/\/ …",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure-based ","type":"text"},{"code":"userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keypath runs on every dispatch, so the value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" live in state — never call into the Keychain from the closure. Hydrate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once; observe state.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Type-safe-Keys","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Type-safe Keys"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare each key once on ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" so the value type travels with the name —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no magic strings at call sites:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == SortOrder {","    static let sortOrder = KVKey<SortOrder>(\"sortOrder\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let lastSeenVersion = KVKey<String>(\"lastSeenVersion\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Then read and write through static-member literals. The compiler enforces","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that the value type matches what you declared:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let theme = store.value(.theme) ?? .system            \/\/ Theme?","store.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","store.setValue(.alphabetical, for: .sortOrder)","store.removeValue(for: .lastSeenVersion)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A typo or wrong type produces a compile error, not a silent miss at runtime.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Centralizing keys on ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" also gives you autocomplete and a single place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to audit your preference surface.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Wiring","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Wiring"},{"anchor":"1-Add-to-your-environment","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"1. Add to your environment"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct AppEnvironment: Sendable {","    var keyValue: any KeyValueStore","","    static func live() -> AppEnvironment {","        AppEnvironment(keyValue: UserDefaultsKeyValueStore())","    }","}"]},{"anchor":"2-Hydrate-at-startup","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"2. Hydrate at startup"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Read once into the initial state — never read mid-cycle from a reducer.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension AppState {","    static func hydrated(from store: any KeyValueStore) -> AppState {","        AppState(","            theme: store.value(.theme) ?? .system,","            sortOrder: store.value(.sortOrder) ?? .alphabetical,","            lastSeenVersion: store.value(.lastSeenVersion)","        )","    }","}","","let env = AppEnvironment.live()","let store = AppStore.configured(state: .hydrated(from: env.keyValue), environment: env)"]},{"anchor":"3-Write-from-an-effect","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"3. Write from an effect"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mutate state in the reducer, return an effect that writes the value:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["case .themeChanged(let theme):","    state.theme = theme","    return { @Sendable _ in","        environment.keyValue.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","    }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no ","type":"text"},{"code":"do\/catch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/setValue(_:for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" does not throw —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder errors are programmer mistakes (e.g. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float.nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so the store logs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them and triggers ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertionFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in DEBUG instead of forcing every effect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to handle an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it can’t act on.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Testing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Inject ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and assert against the same instance:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@Test","@MainActor","func themeChangePersists() async throws {","    let prefs = InMemoryKeyValueStore()","    let env = AppEnvironment(keyValue: prefs)","    let store = AppStore.configured(state: AppState(), environment: env)","","    try await confirmation(expectedCount: 1) { confirm in","        store.send(.themeChanged(.dark))","","        for _ in 0..<50 {","            if prefs.value(.theme) == .dark {","                confirm()","                break","            }","            try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(10))","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Simulate a relaunch.","    let rehydrated = AppState.hydrated(from: prefs)","    #expect(rehydrated.theme == .dark)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tests touching real ","type":"text"},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" should use a fresh per-test suite and tear","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it down explicitly:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let suiteName = \"myapp.tests.\\(UUID().uuidString)\"","let defaults = UserDefaults(suiteName: suiteName)!","defer { defaults.removePersistentDomain(forName: suiteName) }","","let store = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore(suite: defaults)"]},{"anchor":"Reads-Are-For-Hydration","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reads Are For Hydration"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" mid-cycle (inside a reducer) is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anti-pattern. Reducers must be pure and synchronous; reads happen once at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" construction. After hydration, the value lives in state and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downstream code observes state, not the store."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" itself is thread-safe, but a reducer reading while an effect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes creates ordering ambiguity. Hydrate, observe state, write through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effects — that’s the discipline.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Failure-Modes","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Failure Modes"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Missing key"}]},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/value(_:)"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":". Provide a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default at the call site.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decode failure"}]},{"text":" — returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" and logs through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os.Logger"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(subsystem ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"swidux\""},{"text":", category ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"kvstore\""},{"text":"). On startup, behaves identically","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to first launch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encode failure"}]},{"text":" — logged at the same subsystem\/category, then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertionFailure"},{"text":" fires in DEBUG so the bug surfaces during development.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Production builds log and continue; the in-memory state is unchanged. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API does not throw — there is no useful runtime recovery from inside an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effect, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"text":" would just hide the problem.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"AppStorage-Interop","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"@AppStorage Interop"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There is none, by design. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" writes JSON-encoded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" blobs. SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"@AppStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only observes native primitive types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"URL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", raw ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Two parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation channels — Swidux state and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@AppStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — would drift.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux state is the source of truth. Read once at hydration, then observe","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state through the store.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Schema-Migration","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Schema Migration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Out of scope for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". If a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shape changes","type"